 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm skin ellipse containing a 4 5cm well healed scar and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm unremarkable nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail is also present with this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a small REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm cavity  Area surrrounding the biopsy cavity is focally white and focally pink and firm  The biopsy cavity extends to 2 5cm from the closest deep margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma is focally yellow and focally white and grossly unremarkable  Section code  A  representative section of biopsy cavity in relation to deep resection margin B C  biopsy cavity in its entirety D G  additional representative sections of areas surrounding biopsy cavity H I  representative section of breast parenchyma away from biopsy cavity J  representative section of nipple Sectioning of axillary tail reveals eleven soft  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph nodes  Representative sections submitted in cassettes K M  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
