Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 17 CLINICAL DATA  Fifty eight year old female with 1 5cm tumor with positive margins on biopsy from an outside facility  now undergoing partial mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 29                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The skin ellipse contains a vertical scar measuring 3 8cm in length  As denoted by the surgeon  a short stitch marks the superior aspect of the specimen and a long stitch marks the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked entirely in black and then serially section from superior aspect to its inferior aspect to reveal a central hemorrhagic cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm that is within REMOVED_DATE   0 3cm of the anterolateral border of the superior portion of the breast  A predominant gray yellow area of firm consistency measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm extends to within 0 2cm of the posterolateral margin in the superior aspect of the specimen  Continuing superiorly is a firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm at the lateral inked margin  No other gross lesions are identified  Section code  A  biopsy cavity from mid region of specimen with skin ellipse anterior  demonstrating anterolateral margin  B  area of white thickening in superior aspect of the specimen  with posterolateral margin  C  biopsy cavity and lesion at lateral margin  with medial surface removed  D  lesion at posterolateral margin  E  biopsy cavity from mid area of specimen surface removed F G  biopsy cavity  at lateral margin of specimen  in the superior portion  H  lesion in lateral aspect of specimen I  superior margin Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael V Seiden  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 29 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT POSTERIOR LESION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED SURGICAL MARGINS WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION IDENTIFIED  BREAST  RIGHT ANTERIOR LESION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED SURGICAL MARGINS WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION IDENTIFIED  NOTE  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  James F  XxSouthern Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 49 Proofread by  XXSOUTHERN JAMES F                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  ANTERIOR AND POSTERIOR SPECIMENS   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 28     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen consists of two parts  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast posterior lesion  is a piece fibroadipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm with a localizing wire and accompanying X ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white firm area 0 2cm from nearest inked margin  Firm area is submitted in cassettes A through C  the rest in D and E  No frozen section is done  Also received fresh in frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast anterior lesion  is a 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying X ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm white firm area extending to an inked margin  Representative sections is frozen as frozen section  1  This material is saved frozen  The firm area is submitted in cassettes F through K  the rest in cassettes L th