ension  There is a minimal attached tan yellow adipose tissue  The largest lymph node is inked black and bisected  and the lymph nodes are submitted entirely as E  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  superior final shaved margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitch aspect is inked black  and the opposite aspect blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable fatty breast tissue and is entirely submitted as F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and medial final shaved margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  The stitch aspect is inked black  and the opposite aspect blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  is entirely submitted as G  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral final shaved margin   are 3 irregular portions of unremarkable tan pink fibroadipose tissue which aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimen is submitted in toto as H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior final shaved margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  deep final shaved margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a black stitch along one aspect  This aspect is inked black  the opposite aspect blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  and is entirely submitted as J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s nam