R NODULES  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a firm fibrous area within the center  located 0 1cm from the tissue edge  The specimen is entirely frozen as FX 1 and is resubmitted in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan white firm stellate mass which grossly abuts multiple inked resection margins  Representative sections are submitted in B J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  in 2 parts  Labeled  right breast modified radical mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  Overlying the specimen is a 16 x 6cm skin ellipse  that contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 8cm nipple and areola  A 4 0cm long  linear  non healed  non sutured incision is present 3 0cm superolateral to the areola  Beneath this incision is a open  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm biopsy cavity  with a defect leading to the anterior surface of the specimen  located 0 9cm from the deep resection margin  and 7 0cm from the superior resection margin  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by focally firm  tan white and hemorrhagic parenchyma  and contains 2 sutures along its inferior edge  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed of lobulated  yellow  soft adipose tissue with interposed tan white  rubbery  fibrous tissue  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE   2 7cm in greatest dimension  Section Code  K  Biopsy cavity with deep resection margin  L O  Biopsy cavity with surrounding firm area  representative  P  Fibrous area  breast  representative  Q DD  Lymph nodes  Label  left modified radical mastectomy breast with axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  An REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm skin ellipse overlies the specimen  and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm nipple and areola  Sectioning reveals 4 discrete  tan white  scaly  gritty masses  The first is located in the lower outer quadrant  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  and extends to 2 0cm of the deep  and 6 5cm of the inferior margin  The second is present in the mid portion of the lower quadrant  between the outer and inner   measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and extends to 1 0cm from the deep  3 5cm of the inferior  and 0 5cm of the anterior margins  The third is present in the lower outer quadrant  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and extends to 1 5cm of the deep  and 7 0cm of the inferior margin  The fourth mass is located in the upper inner quadrant  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  and extends to 0 6cm of the deep  and 5 0cm of the superior margin  Apart from these 4 discrete masses  an ill defined  3 0cm in diameter fibrous area is present surrounding the first mass  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed of lobulated  soft yellow adipose tissue and scant  tan white fibrous tissue  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in the greatest dimension  Also in the specimen container  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm unremarkable skin ellipse  with underlying fibroadipose tissue measuring up to 2 0cm in thickness  Section Code  EE  Deep margin to mass  1  representative  FF HH  Mass  1  entirely  II JJ  Fibrotic area next to mass  1  representative  KK  Deep margin to mass  2  representative  LL MM  Mass  2 with anterior margin  representative  NN  Mass  2 representative  OO  Deep margin to mass  3  representative  PP RR  Mass  3  representative  SS  Deep margin to mass  4  representative  TT VV  Mass  4  representative  WW  Skin with underlying tissue  separate fragment  representative  XX GGG  Lymph nodes  HHH III Subcutaneous tissue underlying separate skin ellipse  representative  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  PROBABLY DUCTAL  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D      