firmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan yellow to red  lobulated  oriented  irregular piece of fibrofatty breast tissue with a short suture designating the superior margin  and a long suture designating the lateral margin  A localization wire is received in the bag detached from the specimen  The long axis is medial to lateral  and the specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis from the lateral to medial margin to reveal a grossly unremarkable pr enchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from lateral to medial with an en face section of the lateral margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and an en face section of the medial margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells show moderate  2   to strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2 show only a few invasive tumors  insufficient for evaluation of staining of tumor cells  Dr  John Eichhorn has also reviewed these slides and concurs with this interpretation  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained