Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 40 CLINICAL DATA  Excision right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  IN SITU AND INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  NONCASEATING GRANULOMAS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor grows partly as an intracystic papillary carcinoma  so the extent of invasion is difficult to determine  Invasive carcinoma probably spans less than 1 0cm  Ductal carcinoma in situ does not involve tissue adjacent to the mass  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 58                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a 7 x 5 x 3cm breast mass previously opened to reveal a 3cm in greatest diameter cyst filled with hemorrhagic fluid and luminal tan  firm projections  The specimen is inked away from the opened cyst and then sectioned to reveal a  2 to  3cm firm cyst wall enclosing an tan nodular to papillary luminal projection and unremarkable fatty tissue in the remainder of the specimen  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through F with unremarkable tissue in E and F  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
