Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 AUG 95 at 15 51 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer  Biopsy in REMOVED_DATE showed invasive lobular carcinoma 2 8cm                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   WITH ASSOCIATED INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL  WITH PAGETOID SPREAD  SLIDE M   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  FIBROSIS  GRANULATION TISSUE  FAT NECROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND FOAMY MACROPHAGES CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma displays glandular  tubule  formation as well as single cell infiltration  The carcinoma is located adjacent to but not within the previous biopsy site  The glandular pattern differs from the previous carcinoma  see  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and thus probably represents a second primary carcinoma  All margins are free of tumor  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  SOFT TISSUE   LEFT CHEST WALL NODULE    BIOPSY  FRAGMENT OF FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE FAT NECROSIS AND SCANT HEMOSIDERIN LADEN MACROPHAGES  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPHADENECTOMY  LEVEL II    TWO OF TWO LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  HOT SPOT  1  CT   REMOVED_CASE_ID     METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor completely replaces the lymph node  there is no extranodal extension    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  HOT SPOT  1  CT  589    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  WITH FOCAL MICROSCOPIC EXTRANODAL EXTENSION    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  HOT SPOT  1  CT  687    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EXTRANODAL EXTENSION    LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  