 MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 AUG 95 at 09 42    REVISED REMOVED_DATE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left chest wall nodule   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 05cm tan yellow piece of tissue  entirely frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are nine separate parts  Labeled  left axillary lymphadenectomy  level II   is a 1 0cm soft tissue containing two 0 2cm nodules  submitted entirely in cassette B  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  1  ct   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a 1 5cm fatty tissue containing a 1 0cm lymph node and a 0 3cm lymph node  Both lymph nodes are submitted entirely in Cassette C  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  1  ct  589   is a 0 6cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette D  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  1  ct  687   is a 0 6cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette E  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  0  ct  295   is a 0 5cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette F  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  0  ct  186   is a 0 6cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette G  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  hot spot  0  ct  585   is a 1 0cm lymph node  submitted entirely in cassette H  Labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast with a 3 5cm skin ellipse containing a 1 0cm unremarkable nipple  Sectioning revealed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan  firm area parallel and lateral to the nipple and 1 0cm from the deep surgical margin  This area is also stained with a blue dye  SECTION CODE  I  breast tissue  3 0cm medial to the nipple  J  section  1 5cm medial to the nipple  K  firm area  1 0cm lateral to the nipple including posterior surgical margin  L  section  2 0cm lateral to the nipple including anterior m