y signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Rare ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Rare ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells show nuclear staining for estrogen receptor protein  focal cytoplasmic staining for estrogen receptor protein is also present  which is unusual and interpreted as non specific  Uninvolved breast components show scattered estrogen receptor positive cells  which is normal  The progesterone receptor stain was negative  Immunohistochemical stains were performed twice with similar results  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Right   Excision PART B  Breast  Right   Final Superior Margin    Excision PART C  Breast  Right   Final Medial Margin    Excision PART D  Breast  Right   Final Lateral Margin   Excision PART E  Breast  Right   Final Inferior Margin   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
