ibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of breast with a long stitch marking the lateral margin  The short stitch marking the superior margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white stellate firm tumor mass  The tumor is abutting the inferior medial resection margin  0 5cm to the deep margin and 1 5cm to the superior and lateral margins  The remaining tissue is fibrofatty  A section of the tumor is frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette A  Tumor with inferior medial margin in B and C  Tumor with medial and deep margins in D  tumor with deep margin in E  Representative section of the remaining tissue in F and G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axilla  hot spot  Ct 363  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan lymph node bisected and submitted entirely in cassette H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary lymphadenectomy Level