Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 34 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  85    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  MEASURING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SLIDE A   EXTENDS TO THE SURGICAL MARGINS   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  15    SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS MULTIPLE FOCI  EXTENDS TO AN INKED SURGICAL MARGIN  3  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SMALL FOCUS  REMOVED_DATE CM  SLIDE D  PRESENT LESS THAN 1 MM FROM AN INKED SURGICAL MARGIN   SEE NOTE   4  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIPLE FOCI   SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 43 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by