Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 37 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma in situ on biopsy at outside hospital  Slides reviewed at MGH  Rule out invasive carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  LUMPECTOMY  1  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    MICROPAPILLARY AND CRIBRIFORMING TYPE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE MEDIAL INKED MARGIN  2  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2    GRADE REMOVED_DATE SEE NOTE  NOTE  A single unequivocal focus of infiltrating carcinoma  slide G  measures 0 3cm and is present 0 5cm from the medial surgical margin  Two areas on slide A  0 1cm in greatest dimension  and on slide D  0 3cm in greatest dimension  are equivocal for invasion  Drs  Pilch  Rosenberg  Koerner and Sgroi have seen representative slides  Drs  Koerner and Sgroi interpret that the specimen has multiple foci of invasion  3  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIFOCAL  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH ATYPICAL DUCTAL AND LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 35     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast lumpectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overlying skin ellipse  A short stitch is designated superior  a long stitch is designated lateral  Blue ink is applied laterally  Black inked is applied medially  The specimen is sectioned superior to inferior to reveal a 3 0cm nodule  adjacent to the medial posterior margin  which consists of firm  white parenchyma admixed with focal  white tan  gritty tissue  A representative section of the gritty tissue is frozen as FX  1  The remainder is submitted as follows  Section Code A   tissue adjacent to frozen section B F   entirety of the nodule G   superior resection margin  en face H I K L M   parenchyma 1cm inferior to nodule and 1cm superior to inferior resection margin J   inferior resection margin  en face N O   parenchyma 1cm superior to nodule but 1cm inferior from superior resection margin P   FX  1 reprsentative section of mass Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  O R  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
