sed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  tan  yellow  fibrofatty mass with 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin attached  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm biopsy cavity with surrounding ill defined white to tan tissue  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in A  the remainder of tissue is submitted in B through N  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   REACTIVE FIBROSIS  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Carlos Fernandez del castillo  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
