n this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   are two fragments of fibroadipose breast tissue  with the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and the smaller measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  A stitch designates the posterior margin of the largest specimen  A note by the surgeon indicates that the smaller fragment of tissue is additional anterior margin  All specimens are inked black with the posterior surface of the largest specimen inked yellow over black  The additional anterior margin is entirely submitted in cassette A  The largest specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  white to white yellow  firm  nodular area  located in the anterior portion of the largest specimen  within REMOVED_DATE to 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  The nodule has scattered punctate hemorrhage especially at its periphery  The remaining parenchyma is mostly adipose tissue  and unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes B through J  with the nodule in cassettes B through D  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
