case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh and labeled  right breast   is a 23 x 15 x 3 5cm mastectomy specimen with a suture designating axillary tail  The specimen bears a REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm skin ellipse with a central 3 x 3 5cm nipple areolar complex  The lateral aspect of the skin ellipse bears a well healed 3 5cm linear defect and immediately subjacent is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm ovoid non healed defect  Deep to the incision site is a poorly defined firm nodularity approximating 5 x 3 x 2cm  The anterior aspect of the specimen is inked blue  the posterior aspect of the specimen is inked black  Located in the superolateral aspect of the specimen is a 3 x 2cm heterogenous firm yellow tan region which extends to the overlying black inked margin  Deep to the well healed incision is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity consistent with prior surgical site  This lesion is centrally hemorrhagic and peripherally firm and yellow tan with focal peripheral yellow orange punctate irregularities  This cavity extends to 0 1cm from the black inked margin and 2 3cm from the blue inked margin  The remaining parenchyma is focally fibrotic but otherwise grossly unremarkable  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavitary lesion to black inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavitary lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavitary lesion with peripheral orange yellow nodularities   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavitary lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous bands extending anteriorly from cavitary lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous firm region in superolateral aspect of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections distant from lesion  Received fresh and labeled  left breast   is a 22 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm mastectomy specimen bearing a REMOVED_DATE x 6 8cm tan pink skin ellipse with a central 3 x 2 5cm nipple areolar complex  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating axillary tail  There is a well healed curvilinear scar spanning the upper outer quadrants of the areola  The posterior surface is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm defect overlying a cavitary lesion which is 2 4cm in depth  This cavitation extends to 0 3cm from the anterior margin  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior surface is inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal focal fibrosis throughout the specimen  The cavitary lesion is lined by hemorrhagic glistening tissue consistent with granulation tissue  The periphery of the lesion is notable for multiple orange yellow punctate nodularities  2 2cm from the inferolateral extent of the cavitary lesion is a heterogenous REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm red tan nodule  Adjacent to the stitch demarcating the axillary tail is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm nodule with a tan yellow and focally hemorrhagic cut surface  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of axillary nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule adjacent to cavitary lesion  entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial aspect of cavitary lesion with orange yellow punctate nodularities   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavitation to anterior surface   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavitary lesion  black inked margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section distant to cavitary lesion  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Unchecked.
