h this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 MAY 94 at 08 49     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue with a palpable firm mass  The firm mass  which is composed of firm  irregular tan white tissue is REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  and is 0 3cm from an inked surface  Also present is a tan area that extends to an inked margin  Tumor is submitted in cassettes A through D  and all remaining tissue in cassettes E though J  Representative tumor sent for Estrogen receptor study  The frozen section is saved frozen  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                      